# Cloudflare cache rules for this site (see CLAUDE.md, "Caching and cache-busting").
#
# CSS and JS: every page links them with a ?v=<content hash> version (written by inject_header.py), so a
# changed file always gets a new URL. Browsers can therefore keep each version for a year without checking.
#
# HTML pages are left to Cloudflare's default, "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate": browsers check for a new
# copy on every visit, so they always pick up new ?v= links. (No /* rule here on purpose: Cloudflare merges
# the headers of every rule that matches a path, which would clash with the rules below.)
#
# Images keep Cloudflare's default too.

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
